    "provider_frontier": "Eight frozen default calls: checkerboard_level_set and disk_level_set on shapes 256x256,1024x1024,64x64x64,128x64x32. These generators accept shape tuples, not image buffers of different dtypes; outputs are int8. Full public default evaluation, normalization, native admission, allocation, owned scalar/SIMD geometry and output destruction are timed. Checker uses square_size=5; disk uses default integer center and radius=min(shape)*3/8, preserving sqrt/subtract/strict>0. Fresh reference results are verified against the original-first frozen metadata/SHA; full output bytes and metadata then match before timing, with hashes only exported. Unsupported protocols/floating centers/exceptional providers are outside this cohort. All raw samples and losses remain included. This original/current comparison is neither a prior-C++ gain nor full supported-profile qualification."
